                <pb facs="0330" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v02/pg302"/>

                <head>125. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At a meeting of the National Security Council on February 24, Admiral Radford
                    stated that “at four o’clock this morning the Chinese Nationalists had begun to
                    evacuate their forces from Nanchi-San <pb facs="0331" n="303" xml:id="pg303"/>
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">Nan-chi Shan</hi>]. For once he was able to inform
                    the members of the Council of such information before they read it in the press
                    or learned it over the radio. The United States had informed the Chinese
                    Nationalists that it would not assist them in holding Nanchi-San, and in
                    response to this statement they had begun the evacuation.” (Memorandum of
                    discussion by Gleason; Eisenhower Library, Whitman File, NSC Records)</p>
                <p>Telegram 584 from Taipei, February 25, stated that the evacuation of both
                    civilians and military personnel from Nanchi had been completed that morning.
                    (Department of State, Central Files, 793.5/2–2555)</p>
            </div>
